From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:06:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] checkasm/snowdsp: Include intmath before public headers

Checkasm objects are built without HAVE_AV_CONFIG_H. Including snow.h
first reaches common.h through avcodec.h, which installs the generic
av_popcount, av_popcount64 and av_zero_extend aliases. The later
rangecoder.h inclusion reaches x86/intmath.h and redefines them when
POPCNT and BMI2 are enabled.

Include intmath.h before the public headers so common.h sees the chosen
implementations. This fixes the redefinition warnings reported with gcc
15.2 with -march=x86-64-v3 without changing all checkasm objects or
making the architecture header retain the generic fallbacks.

Signed-off-by: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
---
 tests/checkasm/snowdsp.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/tests/checkasm/snowdsp.c b/tests/checkasm/snowdsp.c
index 99cfae679e204c85b42b1e7140aaa297be8a186a..aa031e4d85104a60d217efe06ee44b26d96e4927 100644
--- a/tests/checkasm/snowdsp.c
+++ b/tests/checkasm/snowdsp.c
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
 #include <stdint.h>
 #include <string.h>
 
+#include "libavutil/intmath.h"
 #include "libavutil/intreadwrite.h"
 #include "libavutil/macros.h"
 #include "libavutil/mem_internal.h"
